      "content": "that's an interesting point about the fascination part. but sometimes the way they're described doesn't feel very \"respectful\" though. like there are parts where they're basically described as being less than human or just like part of the jungle. if a modern author wrote like that today, it would be called straight up racism. why is it okay to treat it as \"nuanced\" or \"poetic\" in this book? doesn't that kind of minimize the actual harm of those descriptions?",
